        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>At 14, Max’s heart stopped during a basketball game. Five years after her son's death, Fiona Connolly recalls pleading with hospital staff to save her son. 'I said, \"This is Max. His name is Max, and I really need you to to do what you do really well, and please just get him back to life.”' Research suggests one person under 35 experiences a sudden cardiac arrest every day in Australia, and studies put the fatality rate at 90%, making it one of the biggest killers of young people. The first symptom of a sudden cardiac death can be, as in the case of Max, that the heart simply stops.</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/ng-interactive/2026/jun/21/sudden-cardiac-arrest-leading-cause-death-young-people\">‘A child goes to bed and doesn’t wake up’: the families left in shock after the sudden death of their healthy children</a></p></li><li><p><em>In Australia, support for people who are grieving is available from </em><a href=\"https://griefline.org.au/\"><em>Griefline</em></a><em> on 1300 845 745</em></p></li></ul> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/video/2026/aug/10/maxs-heart-stopped-while-playing-basketball-it-was-a-case-of-sudden-cardiac-arrest-video\">Continue reading...</a>"
